---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Notes" description="Mathematical notes, research explanations, and selected writing by John Rick Manzanares.">
  <header class="page-hero shell">
    <p class="kicker">Notes</p>
    <h1>A notebook for ideas that need more room.</h1>
    <p class="page-intro">
      Some ideas are too explanatory for a paper and too substantial for a short post. This section is
      where I want to develop them carefully, with definitions, examples, and enough context to stand on their own.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section section-soft">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Three kinds of notes</p>
          <h2>Different writing, one notebook.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          The categories are meant to separate mathematical exposition from research commentary and personal writing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="path-grid">
        <div class="path-card path-card-static">
          <span>Mathematics</span>
          <strong>Definitions, examples, and proofs</strong>
          <p>Notes in topology, analysis, operators, and related mathematical foundations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="path-card path-card-static">
          <span>Research notes</span>
          <strong>Methods explained outside the paper format</strong>
          <p>Longer explanations of algorithms, modelling choices, scientific computing, and reproducibility.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="path-card path-card-static">
          <span>Academic life</span>
          <strong>Personal writing and reflection</strong>
          <p>Selected writing about research, movement between places, and life in academia.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Academic life</p>
          <h2>Selected writing</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          The journal that once occupied the home page now has its own reading space.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline">
        <article class="timeline-card">
          <time>Updated 16 May 2025</time>
          <h3>Strangers and Struggles in a New World</h3>
          <p>
            Notes written during the first year of moving abroad for doctoral research, from November 2024
            to May 2025.
          </p>
          <div class="inline-links">
            <a href="/notes/strangers-and-struggles-in-a-new-world/">Read article →</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-soft">
    <div class="shell compact-callout">
      <p class="kicker">Writing principle</p>
      <h2>Make the note useful without the conversation that produced it.</h2>
      <p>
        Mathematical notes should define their objects, state assumptions, and explain notation. Research notes
        should distinguish established results from interpretation and work still in progress.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
